WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.451
Grace was at the park.

2
00:00:05.452 --> 00:00:13.628
Today was her cousin's dragon boat race!

3
00:00:13.629 --> 00:00:17.837
"I have to meet my team now," her cousin, Peter, said.

4
00:00:17.838 --> 00:00:20.185
"The race starts soon."

5
00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:26.695
"Good luck!" said Grace.

6
00:00:26.696 --> 00:00:30.177
Grace and Dad walked toward the river.

7
00:00:30.178 --> 00:00:35.151
"Look!" Grace pointed to the boats on the water.

8
00:00:35.152 --> 00:00:39.822
They all had tall dragon heads and tails.

9
00:00:39.823 --> 00:00:45.319
"In China there's a dragon boat festival every spring," said Dad.

10
00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:50.468
"Why are all the boats shaped like dragons?" asked Grace.

11
00:00:50.469 --> 00:00:58.012
"Long ago farmers believed that dragons would bring rain," said Dad.

12
00:00:58.013 --> 00:01:03.803
"Rice needs lots of rain to grow."

13
00:01:03.804 --> 00:01:07.716
Just then Grace saw Peter with his team.

14
00:01:07.717 --> 00:01:10.087
He looked worried.

15
00:01:10.088 --> 00:01:14.423
"One of our paddlers is sick," Peter said.

16
00:01:14.424 --> 00:01:17.989
"We can't race."

17
00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:21.344
"I can paddle," said Grace.

18
00:01:21.345 --> 00:01:23.881
"Thanks, Grace," Peter said.

19
00:01:23.882 --> 00:01:27.699
"But you don’t know how to paddle a dragon boat."

20
00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:33.732
Grace shrugged. "I know how to row a canoe."

21
00:01:33.733 --> 00:01:36.461
The boat captain heard Grace.

22
00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:38.264
"Let's give her a chance.

23
00:01:38.265 --> 00:01:41.428
The race starts in a few minutes!"

24
00:01:41.429 --> 00:01:51.235
"Okay," Peter said.

25
00:01:51.236 --> 00:01:53.537
Grace jumped into the boat.

26
00:01:53.538 --> 00:01:58.114
Peter gave her a paddle and showed her what to do.

27
00:01:58.115 --> 00:02:02.806
Then a horn blew.

28
00:02:02.807 --> 00:02:06.798
The dragon boats were off!

29
00:02:06.799 --> 00:02:12.873
Boom! Boom! The captain stood in front with a drum.

30
00:02:12.874 --> 00:02:19.640
Each time she banged the drum, the twenty paddlers paddled.

31
00:02:19.641 --> 00:02:22.621
A boy in the back steered.

32
00:02:22.622 --> 00:02:27.586
Boom! Whoosh! Boom! Whoosh!

33
00:02:27.587 --> 00:02:32.764
The dragon boat flew over the water.

34
00:02:32.765 --> 00:02:41.336
The crowd roared from the shore.

35
00:02:41.337 --> 00:02:49.987
Grace cheered as their boat zipped across the finish line.

36
00:02:49.988 --> 00:02:52.784
"Third place!" cried Peter.

37
00:02:52.785 --> 00:03:03.326
"Thanks, Grace. You saved the day!"

